      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Place the carrot rounds in a medium saucepan and cover with cold salted water. Bring to the boil and cook for 8-10 minutes until just tender but still holding their shape. They should not be soft enough to mash."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Drain the carrots well and leave them to steam dry in the colander for a few minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Whisk together the olive oil, lemon juice, harissa, honey, ground cumin, ground coriander and black pepper in a large bowl."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the warm carrots to the dressing and toss well to coat. Leave to cool to room temperature, tossing occasionally so the carrots absorb the dressing as they cool."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stir through most of the fresh coriander and parsley. Taste and adjust the seasoning, adding more lemon juice or harissa as needed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Transfer to a serving plate. Scatter over the remaining herbs and the toasted sesame seeds. Serve at room temperature."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "question": "The carrots are too soft"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Check the carrots at 7 minutes. They should be just tender with a little resistance when pierced with a knife. Overcooked carrots lose their texture after being dressed, so err on the side of undercooking."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "question": "The dressing is not clinging to the carrots"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make sure the carrots are well drained and still warm when you add them to the dressing. Warm carrots absorb dressing much more readily than cold ones. Toss them thoroughly and let them sit for at least 10 minutes before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "question": "The salad is too spicy"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Balance the heat with a little more honey and lemon juice. Adding extra chopped fresh coriander also mellows the harissa. Next time, reduce the harissa to half a tablespoon and add more gradually."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Spiced carrot salad is a fixture of the Moroccan table, appearing alongside other cooked salads as part of a spread served before the main course. It is one of those dishes that looks simple but is carefully calibrated between sweet, sharp, warm and hot. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "harissa-term"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Harissa"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is not always used in traditional versions, which more commonly use cumin alone, but the combination has become widespread across Morocco and the Moroccan diaspora in France. The salad keeps well in the fridge for 2-3 days and improves with time."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
